1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:02,670
Behold,

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:07,604
the village of Windnight's Lot, nestled
in a valley and ringed by daunting cliffs.

3
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:09,960
A castle dominates the landscape,

4
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:13,117
built in the Middle Ages as
a proving ground for knights.

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:18,180
It houses prisoners who toil underground,
mining coal as pennants for their crimes.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,012
Fishing and farming provide
sustenance and commerce alike.

7
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:26,244
Five hundred and seventeen souls
call the sleepy bird their home.

8
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:29,780
But how few shall remain
when the carnage is done?

9
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,140
Thank you for listening.

10
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:50,479
Kinoto!

11
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,500
Farmers sing to the harvest.

12
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,077
Thus far, all is well.

13
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:18,940
However, Dio lurks in the
shadows waiting to strike.

14
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,520
What happened?

15
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:26,617
Well, Speedwagon has been begging
me to share in your power.

16
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:29,717
I meant to help him create
just a little bit of harmone,

17
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,737
as I did that first day with you.

18
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:33,320
It seems I was too rough.

19
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,798
Did my finger slip?

20
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,906
Un miliai, you're discusi,
my dear Speedwagon.

21
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,720
In English, please!

22
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,737
El culprit is a lad, it would seem.

23
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:54,437
His crime was well planned.

24
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:56,377
I salute the boy's ingenuity.

25
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:59,517
How come you two are heaping
praise on that little imp?

26
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,157
He's making off with every
pound we have to our names.

27
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,957
Oi, bring it back!

28
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,357
Yes, he took our money.

29
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,177
But think how he might be able to help.

30
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:08,090
Agreed.

31
00:03:08,173 --> 00:03:11,780
A guide who knows the lay of
the land would not be unwelcome.

32
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:15,840
Um... Yeah!

33
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,100
What the...?

34
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:32,360
He's walking on it!

35
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:40,077
Jojo, your shoes are getting wet.

36
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:43,513
Try to bolster your haamon
for the sake of your wardrobe.

37
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,540
Ah, that was a nice diminuendo.

38
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:02,937
Your overdrive passed through
the rocks as smooth as silk.

39
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:05,317
Do you think I struck
the right spot, Baron?

40
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:08,357
No, but a couple of paces
to the left should do it.

41
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,100
Two pounds says I'm right.

42
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:15,210
What?

43
00:04:15,293 --> 00:04:16,123
It shocked me!

44
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:18,340
Molto Bone.

45
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:21,060
What happened? Who are you?

46
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:22,613
Why are you holding me?

47
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:24,253
Lad, are you all right?

48
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:26,377
The force shouldn't have
hurt you that badly.

49
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:28,048
Did I use too much hormone?

50
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:32,940
I'd guess we were meant to give chase
when he took our bag. Look around.

51
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:37,380
This is a graveyard!

52
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:44,580
It's no accident that we now find
ourselves held by these restless cadavers,

53
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:45,650
my friends.

54
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:51,760
Our young thief, he was hypnotized and made
to lure us here. There, Jojo! It's him!

55
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:53,570
Huh?

56
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,640
The sun is gone.

57
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:04,100
You will not live to
see it rise once more.

58
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,630
Dio!

59
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,900
Why are they crawling out?

60
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:16,417
I've been trying to steal my spine
leading up to this little tete-a-tete,

61
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:19,137
but it's like the Grim Reaper's
breathing down me neck.

62
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:20,380
I'm all a sweat.

63
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:25,337
How am I supposed to find my courage when
that monster's staring right at us, huh?

64
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:29,244
Sir Joestar loved him, and all he
got for his troubles was death.

65
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:30,790
Listen, you.

66
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,620
You're gonna pay for it.

67
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,877
This is Dio Brando.

68
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:40,489
He and his minions have no power to
attack us while we stand in the daylight,

69
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:43,197
but here in a field of
darkness and carrion?

70
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:47,117
He thinks us easy prey
ripe for the taking at any

71
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:51,180
moment a creature of such
guile must not have the mask!

72
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:55,060
Somehow we will purge
the world of this evil.

73
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,388
What do they call you that?

74
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:06,790
Poco?

75
00:06:06,873 --> 00:06:09,160
Well, Poco, hang on tight.

76
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:10,797
It's time for us to go.

77
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,940
Jojo, this way! Lead on!

78
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:21,380
Zoom punch!

79
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,160
Dio Brando.

80
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:39,400
Jojo and Speedwagon have told me much.

81
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:44,040
To the mask that allows you to act
out your evil heart, I say only this.

82
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,060
This time, I break you.

83
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:49,420
Hey, bambino!

84
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:52,717
It's easy to be cocky when you're
up there out of harm's way.

85
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:53,720
Come and fight!

86
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,920
You dare to address me thus, insect.

87
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:59,080
I, the pinnacle of creation.

88
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,220
To mere humans, I am like unto a god.

89
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:05,620
So why would I cavort down
in the filth with you?

90
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:14,100
Me almost knocked me off my
feet with a blast of pure hate.

91
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:16,960
Already this Dio has the soul of a tyrant.

92
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:20,580
All of the scars from my
battle with Jojo have healed.

93
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:22,720
All save this one.

94
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:24,220
Come, Charlatan.

95
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:28,300
Relinquish your blood, that I
may erase this imperfection.

96
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:33,560
Tell me, to undo your injuries, how
many innocent lives did you consume?

97
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:34,797
I don't know.

98
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:38,233
How many loaves of bread have
you eaten in your lifetime?

99
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,340
What are you doing?

100
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:47,420
I will take him home!

101
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,540
Your doom is nigh, Dio!

102
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,030
Hail!

103
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,680
Solar Hormone, pierce the night!

104
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:08,380
Sunlight, yellow, overdrive!

105
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:10,440
He did it!

106
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,940
His Hormone is moving its way up Diozor!

107
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:20,800
Consider this an eclipse.

108
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:22,460
Your hand!

109
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:25,260
It's freezing me!

110
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,000
It's simple, really.

111
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:36,833
For Hamon to work, blood must flow
through this arm with which you hit me.

112
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:41,660
I froze the very blood in your veins,
rendering your attack powerless.

113
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:48,000
I have mastery of my body in ways
that you can't even begin to dream.

114
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:51,897
You see, I just vaporized
the moisture in my left arm.

115
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:54,497
The force of it pulled in
all heat in the immediate

116
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:58,860
area freezing your arm
in the process and now?

117
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:03,497
Time for the coup de grace!

118
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:07,874
This punch is going to shatter your
arm and your skull like a windowpane!

119
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,120
Think again!

120
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:14,267
I'm ending your reign
of terror here and now!

121
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:18,637
Your blood I can feel the
evil coursing through it.

122
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,040
Stop it.

123
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,357
You're going to set me all a-tremble.

124
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,040
Masterful block by the by.

125
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:26,300
For the moment, your mentor lives.

126
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:29,380
I didn't think you had it in you. Jojo!

127
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:37,220
That said, if you keep cutting in like
this, I'm liable to lose my temper.

128
00:09:37,560 --> 00:09:38,390
Terra, now!

129
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,720
It's useless! Yes!

130
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:51,120
As you can see, by freezing my arm,
your puny attack had nowhere to go.

131
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:55,040
If you think Hamon will save
you, you are sorely mistaken.

132
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:57,337
His strength is like
nothing I've ever witnessed.

133
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:59,960
This fiend is our equal many times over.

134
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:03,620
Wait, he's about to freeze
Jojo's arm, just like mine!

135
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,765
Come what may, I can't
let harm before the lad!

136
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:14,720
Barron Zeppeli!

137
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:21,240
Tor, this ain't happening!

138
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,760
My hand's cold as ice.

139
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,040
Every nerve is crying out in pain.

140
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:35,137
The skin on my fingers is peeling.

141
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:36,577
He removed the moisture.

142
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:38,954
The Baron's arm is in a pretty bad way.

143
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:41,677
Gangrene will take it if we
don't get the blood flowing.

144
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:42,780
What do we do?

145
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:45,237
Homo's the only weapon in our arsenal.

146
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,100
How do we stand against him?

147
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:52,040
So anemic, this parlor trick of yours.

148
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:55,040
You should save your breath.

149
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,760
Is it an earthquake?

150
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:03,691
You're going to need that air for all
the screaming I have in store for you.

151
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:05,680
Tarkus! Blueford!

152
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:08,240
Arise and fight at my command!

153
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:13,720
Let their cries of anguish resound,
so that all may know my glory!

154
00:11:33,340 --> 00:11:35,281
Where'd he take up these bruises?

155
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:39,940
Poco, get to safety!

156
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:43,440
These are knights,

157
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:49,280
casualties of Queen Elizabeth's fatal
machinations in the mid-1500s against Mary,

158
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,659
Queen of Scotland.

159
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:52,120
Heed me well.

160
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,300
I find these humans vexing.

161
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,127
I order you to destroy them.

162
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:57,520
I care not how.

163
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,740
Tell me I'm dreaming!

164
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:05,239
That big one broke the
boulder with a single finger!

165
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:07,429
They are waiting for Jojo.

166
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:08,940
He's their main target.

167
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:15,057
He's a warrior, but he
can't handle both of them.

168
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,817
If only my blood would
start moving a little bit.

169
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,900
Then what, Baron?

170
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:21,677
Then I could heal my arm
a little with Harmon.

171
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:24,936
How am I supposed to thaw
this damnable thing in time?

172
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:32,717
If it's heat you need, Speedwagon's
feeling right charitable this evening.

173
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:33,630
What?

174
00:12:33,713 --> 00:12:34,811
So you have a plan, then?

175
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:38,660
In a pinch I figured this'll do ya!

176
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,460
You selfless idiot!

177
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:44,737
Heard they treat frostbite in
the arctic by cutting open a

178
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:48,585
seal and sticking the frozen hand
a foot into the poor blighter!

179
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:52,900
Zoom punch! Aye, pest!

180
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:54,278
Give me your blood!

181
00:12:59,000 --> 00:12:59,830
His hair!

182
00:12:59,913 --> 00:13:01,527
He's using it to feed on me!

183
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,920
Speedwagon, you don't have to do this.

184
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:06,395
With all due respect,

185
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:11,168
I'd be buggered before I let harm come
to you or Jojo while I can lend a hand.

186
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,697
If he can drink my blood through this,

187
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:17,486
then perhaps it will serve as a
conduit for my hormone as well.

188
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:20,100
Sunlight yellow overdrive!

189
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:22,900
Nothing happened.

190
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:26,817
Have I already lost too much vitality
to make my hormone effective?

191
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:29,060
I may have sold you short, Amico.

192
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,400
I thought you would run
when things got truly dire.

193
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:33,590
Me despiace.

194
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:37,688
Baron, if we live through this,
you and me are right as rain.

195
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:47,077
I need to get my arm working.

196
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,177
There's no way he can take them alone.

197
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:52,757
Highballing that sword freezes
me up worse than you just did.

198
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:57,217
Jojo's well over six feet tall, but next
to that thingy might as well be Tom Thumb.

199
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:59,797
Look at the face on
that one, and that one!

200
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,457
He's the bleeding minotaur!

201
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:05,837
I can read people like a book, and
these two are full-a-story speed wagon?

202
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:08,096
don't want to hear, thank you kindly.

203
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:13,620
You should be honored to perish at the
hands of these men, Tarkus and Bluford.

204
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:17,020
Bow to my will, O warriors of yore.

205
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:22,600
In the mid-16th century, two women
waged war for the Crown of England.

206
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:25,960
the cunning Queen Elizabeth I, a Tudor,

207
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:29,560
and the beautiful Mary
Stuart, Queen of Scots.

208
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:34,689
The most steadfast of her vassals were
the great knights Tarkus and Bluford.

209
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:39,665
They had lost their families, without a
purpose to center them, a raison d 'etre.

210
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:40,940
They were adrift.

211
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:45,060
The dutiful man seeks respite,
not in the vagaries of romance,

212
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,515
but in something larger and ineffable.

213
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,780
In Mary they found just that.

214
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:54,822
They swore to serve and honor the young
queen, even at the cost of their own lives.

215
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:59,640
But one day, Mary's husband,
Lord Darnley, was found murdered.

216
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:04,560
Seeing a chance to strike, Elizabeth
blamed Mary for Darnley's death.

217
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,680
The people turned against Mary.

218
00:15:07,140 --> 00:15:10,420
She was caught and imprisoned
in a series of castles.

219
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:14,572
Tarkus and Bluford fought like
lions to free their queen.

220
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:18,785
So fearsome were they, Elizabeth
approached them with a bargain.

221
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,657
Surrender and bring an
end to this bloodshed.

222
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:26,377
Grant us but this one thing
and we will spare Mary's life.

223
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:30,140
If our lives can buy the
Queen her freedom, I accept!

224
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,400
I've no regrets.

225
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:37,040
They went to Elizabeth
and sealed their fate.

226
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:43,140
You think you're so selfless, don't you?

227
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,117
Well, you're losing
your hands for nothing.

228
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,837
Your precious Mary's already worm food?

229
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:52,180
Go ahead, take a look over by that
wall if you're having your doubts.

230
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:54,840
Not so royal now, is she?

231
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,940
Elizabeth, you serpent!

232
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:05,900
You played us false and
murdered Mary anyway!

233
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:11,900
I die this day, but my hatred for you and
your wretched family will live forever!

234
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:13,880
Curse is on you, Queen!

235
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:20,940
And thus, they went to their end.

236
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:24,480
Legend has it that Tarukas'
neck was stiff with fury,

237
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:28,880
and the headsman broke many an axe
before the task was finally done.

238
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:30,260
For his part,

239
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:33,357
Bluford's hair coiled around
the executioner's feet,

240
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:36,060
the peerless locks
slicing the man's flesh.

241
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:41,257
The story of these brave knights' betrayal
seems to have struck a chord with me.

242
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:45,517
From the earth I called them to wreak
their vengeance all these centuries later.

243
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,780
Such is the power at my command.

244
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:50,900
In life they were fearsome.

245
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,746
In death they are invincible.

246
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,600
We have sworn fealty to Lord Dio.

247
00:16:56,780 --> 00:16:59,133
We have come to lay waste to this world.

248
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:01,220
It is a place without redemption.

249
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:06,040
That hate they felt when they
died, it had 300 years to ferment.

250
00:17:09,140 --> 00:17:12,597
Dio's turned the flower of
knighthood into vengeful monsters.

251
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:14,504
Keep your wits about you, Jojo.

252
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:20,120
Hormone within me, come to my aid!

253
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:23,720
Scarlet Overdrive!

254
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:29,260
Look at that power!

255
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:33,940
He looks so calm, but I know
they ain't far from his thoughts.

256
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:37,220
All that he's lost, and
what he's rediscovered.

257
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:40,020
Godspeed, you brave bastard!

258
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:43,737
Methinks this boy is
a champion of his day.

259
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:48,200
He shall make the perfect target upon
which to practice the art of war.

260
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,680
This one's flesh belongs to me.

261
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:55,860
Oh, yes.

262
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:59,820
I can smell his delicious
cartilage already. Another zombie?

263
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,640
He is our foe.

264
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:05,140
Get thee gone from here, you gluttony.

265
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:10,600
He moves with infernal speed.

266
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:15,700
Milord Dio, in this young man I do
sense a great reservoir of spirit.

267
00:18:15,980 --> 00:18:21,360
I humbly petition you for the right to face
him in soul combat and strike him down.

268
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:23,100
As you will then.

269
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:25,620
Tarkus, this one here's mine.

270
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:28,877
That's Bluford the Black Knight.

271
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:32,937
He was known to be a flawless fighter
and he was utterly devoid of mercy.

272
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:35,597
Just watching him put one
foot in front of the other,

273
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,717
I can tell he's no one to tangle with.

274
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:42,980
Back in my school days, we learned
about this man, he and Tarkus.

275
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:46,140
And now, he returns from
the dead to kill me?

276
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,540
Relax your muscles, Jojo.

277
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:51,040
Breathe steadily, no matter what!

278
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,350
What's this?

279
00:18:57,620 --> 00:18:59,760
He's got both hands behind his back!

280
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:02,117
Bluford is giving nothing away!

281
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,788
Which one is his sword arm?

282
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:05,410
Neither.

283
00:19:05,493 --> 00:19:06,677
His hair wields the blade.

284
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:08,340
No, but...

285
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,580
You've a keen eye, my boy.

286
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:17,420
My hair's dance macabre has
claimed many. Have at thee!

287
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:19,150
Shoujo!

288
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,060
Oh no!

289
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:26,164
He's at a serious disadvantage.

290
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:28,440
No air to breathe means no harmone.

291
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:29,860
We have to help him.

292
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:32,340
What now, this brute?

293
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:34,000
Damn, he needs us.

294
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:36,414
And we can't lift a finger to save him.

295
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:38,990
Hmph.

296
00:19:39,073 --> 00:19:40,340
Jojo's as good as dead.

297
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:42,639
He can't touch Blueford underwater.

298
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:43,780
I will go.

299
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:46,119
Here, there is nothing left to see.

300
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:50,480
And now, I will transform this
sleepy village into a necropolis!

301
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,957
The zombies I create will devour England

302
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:56,920
like a plague with the
world soon to follow!

303
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,920
I need to breathe.

304
00:20:06,260 --> 00:20:07,848
I need to generate hormone.

305
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,840
Just a single breath.

306
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:12,797
Go, boy, and make for
the surface if you can.

307
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:14,760
I suffer not for want of air,

308
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:18,017
but my armor leaves me sorely
encumbered under the water.

309
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:19,500
A duel between heroes.

310
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:22,428
If you're lucky, you
can beat me to the top.

311
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,157
Come, you'll drown if you tarry.

312
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:27,440
act, and quickly.

313
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:29,160
Can I make it?

314
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:31,653
Will I just get dragged down to my doom?

315
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,500
I get one chance.

316
00:20:37,180 --> 00:20:39,737
As death readied himself
for another victim,

317
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:42,526
Jojo felt a wellspring
of resolve burst forth.

318
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,020
His lungs screaming for breath,

319
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:49,122
an ordinary man would mindlessly
claw his way towards the surface.

320
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,297
But Jojo knew better than that.

321
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:55,600
Instead, he turned and swam
down, deeper into the abyss.

322
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,070
He's mad!

323
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:58,513
He's going deeper down!

324
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:01,520
What's this?

325
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:04,877
Danny's grabbed hold of your toy
pistol and won't give it back.

326
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,957
You're trying to take it away from him.

327
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:08,099
That's the reason.

328
00:21:08,420 --> 00:21:09,655
Change your strategy.

329
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,960
Try giving it to him instead.

330
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:18,280
We're Night's Lot.

331
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:20,040
It's a coal mining town.

332
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:23,006
That means collapsed
tunnels and sunken earth.

333
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:25,270
There!

334
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:29,544
If I'm right, there should be air
trapped underneath these rocks!

335
00:21:30,180 --> 00:21:31,240
I've found it!

336
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:34,940
With just one breath, my blood
is generating hormone again!

337
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:37,780
That's impossible!

338
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:40,300
Prepare yourself, servant of evil!

339
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:42,080
The tables have turned!

340
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:45,541
Down here, my hormone will
hit you all the harder!

341
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:47,790
Underwater...

342
00:21:47,873 --> 00:21:51,340
Turquoise Blue Overdrive!

343
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:07,960
I'll be the roundabout.

344
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:12,037
The words will make you out or not?

345
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:15,960
You spent the day your way.

346
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:19,997
Calling money while you feel the sun.

347
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:21,700
And in and out the valley.

348
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:26,100
In and out the lake.

349
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:29,597
Moms come out of the sky.

350
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:31,320
We stand there.

351
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:36,457
Why might I know we'll be there?

352
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:38,040
We'll see you!

353
00:22:40,660 --> 00:22:42,817
Don't you say that we'll be there?

354
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,360
You'll be there too.

355
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:49,817
24 before I let you sing.

356
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:52,640
I'll be there with you.

357
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:30,560
Blufrid is a mess!

358
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:32,557
I just hit them until they fall to pieces!

359
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:33,797
This pain is nothing!

360
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:36,417
The day will come when this
will be the death of you.

361
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:37,557
Life magnetism!

362
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,020
Overdrive!
